Title: CI/CD Automation with Docker and Kubernetes using DevOps Tools
Problem Statement
An organization wants to automate the build and deployment of a containerized web application using a simplified DevOps workflow.

As a DevOps Engineer, you must implement a working CI/CD pipeline that demonstrates hands-on knowledge of Git, Docker, Ansible, Jenkins, Terraform, and Kubernetes. 

The focus is on automation and integration, not on complex infrastructure or production hardening.

 
Infrastructure Overview 
You will work with three machines only:

Machine Name	Role
ci-master	Ansible Master + Jenkins Server
ci-agent	Jenkins Agent (Docker enabled)
k8s-node	Single-node Kubernetes Cluster
Kubernetes can be installed as single-node

(control-plane + worker on same machine).

Tasks to Be Performed
1. Git – Source Code Management

Create a Git repository.
Push:
Dockerfile
Jenkinsfile
Ansible playbook
Terraform configuration
Kubernetes YAML files
2. Ansible – Configuration Management
From ci-master:
Install Jenkins and Java on ci-master
Install Docker and Java on ci-agent
Verify services are running
3. Jenkins – CI Pipeline
Configure Jenkins using a Jenkinsfile from Git.
Pipeline should:
Pull code from Git
Build a Docker image
Docker image must display:(PRT – CI/CD Completed Successfully”)
4. Terraform – Infrastructure Provisioning
Using Terraform, provision one instance:
k8s-node
Execute:
terraform init
terraform apply
5. Kubernetes – Deployment
Install Kubernetes on k8s-node
Create:
Deployment
Service
Deploy the Docker image built by Jenkins.
Verify the application is running.
 
Evaluation Rubric (Total: 20 Marks)
Section	Criteria	Marks
Git	Repository contains all required files	3 Marks
Ansible	Correct configuration applied on both nodes	4 Marks
Jenkins	Pipeline successfully builds Docker image	5 Marks
Terraform	Infrastructure provisioning completed successfully	3 Marks
Kubernetes	Application deployed and accessible	5 Marks
Total		20 Marks
Submission Requirements
Git repository link
Screenshots/logs of:
Jenkins pipeline execution
Terraform apply
Kubernetes pod and service status
Application output in browser
